    {
      "text": "This guide provides information on configuring webhooks using ServiceNow for alerts in Risk360. This article provides a sample configuration that can be built on per user requirements. The following ServiceNow webhook sample configuration uses a ServiceNow developer configuration."
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure webhook using ServiceNow:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Create a ServiceNow developer account at https://developer.servicenow.com/.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Create a developer instance.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "This instance automatically hibernates, so you must wake it every 24 hours. Also, the instance is reclaimed if you don’t use it for 10 days.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Filter Navigator search window on the left sidebar, enter rest.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Under Scripted Web Services, click Scripted REST APIs.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          27
        ],
        [
          35,
          53
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click New at the top of the page to create a new resource.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Enter the API name and click Submit.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 6,
      "strong": [
        [
          29,
          35
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The API appears on the page.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click the API name to open it.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 7
    },
    {
      "item": "At the bottom of the page, under the Resources tab, select New.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 8,
      "strong": [
        [
          37,
